.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Entry point for the 42sh unit test suite\&. 


.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
pulgamecanica (arosado-)
.RE
.PP
Run with: \fRmake test\fP
.SS "How to Graduate a Test"
.IP "\(bu" 2
1\&. Implement the module under \fRsrcs/MODULE/\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
2\&. Add \fR-DTEST_MODULE_ENABLED\fP to \fRTEST_FLAGS\fP in the root Makefile\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
3\&. Verify all MU_ASSERT lines pass with \fRmake test\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
4\&. When permanently green:
.br
 Delete \fR#ifdef\fP / \fR#else\fP / \fR#endif\fP in \fRtests/test_module\&.c\fP\&.
.br
 Delete \fR#ifdef\fP / \fR#endif\fP around MU_RUN() below\&.
.br
 Remove \fR-DTEST_MODULE_ENABLED\fP from the root Makefile\&.
.br
 The test then compiles and runs unconditionally forever\&. 
.PP

.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "void test_dlist_suite (void )"
Run all doubly-linked list assertions\&.

.PP
Builds a three-node list \fR[1 <-> 2 <-> 3]\fP, verifies size, forward and backward links, sentinel NULL values at both ends, then calls ft_dlstclear() and asserts the head pointer is NULL afterwards\&. 
.SS "void test_history_suite (void )"
Run all history module assertions\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
history_file_path: $HISTFILE takes priority\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
history_file_path: falls back to $HOME/\&.sh_history when $HISTFILE unset\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
history_save / history_load round-trip preserves all entries\&. 
.PP

.SS "void test_lexer_suite (void )"

.PP
Run all lexer unit tests\&. Called by \fBtest_runner\&.c\fP via MU_RUN(test_lexer_suite)\&. 
.SS "void test_list_suite (void )"
Run all singly-linked list assertions\&.

.PP
Builds an append-order list \fR[alpha(1) -> beta(2) -> gamma(3)]\fP, verifies ft_lstsize() and forward traversal via \fR->next\fP, then exercises ft_lstdel() (freeing all nodes with del_dummy) and asserts the head pointer is NULL afterwards\&.

.PP
A second sub-test uses ft_lstadd() (prepend) to verify that two nodes inserted as \fR[first, second]\fP are stored as \fR[second -> first]\fP in the list\&.

.PP
.RS 4
\fBPrecondition:\fP \fRLibft/srcs/ft_stdlib/\fP must be compiled and linked\&. 
.RE
.PP

